  "notes": "Actual client calibration draft: visible draw gap after open melds; four rotated public meld regions. Pon source uses the single sideways tile position only for a known three-tile pon; left/middle/right layout verified against public call sequences and WRC section 8.12. Touching groups require a unique identity partition. Kan structure/source and gameplay buttons remain incomplete; calibrated=false. Draft 7 reuses all existing region coordinates and training images; v4 fallback handles specular stripes only after failed primary geometry. Three frozen train SVMs may verify an unknown existing template proposal; incomplete regions still pause. Stage 2 gate remains unpassed. Pjura integration: pinned 34-class ViT ONNX is primary for tile identity; legacy colour evidence resolves fives and matching templates alone confirm orientation. Enabled by explicit user request irrespective of acceptance metrics. No local test training or threshold tuning. Draft-14: top/left/right river rects grown away from each grid origin (origins unchanged) to hold four rows plus a riichi tile; own river was grown in draft-13. Draft-15: buttons.banner_rect reads coloured reaction banners (吃 green, 碰 teal, 和 red) up to three slots left of 跳過. Draft-16: meld_left grown upward (to y=410) and right for a second call; blue-backed left-wall bodies at its top are excluded (理和鸣切 panel excluded); river_self max width 68 for a sideways riichi tile (measured 59x47). Draft-17: uncertain clearly sideways identities may be verified by both quarter-turns, three train-only glyph SVMs and their nearest-reference votes; original ViT, confidence threshold and five-colour policy unchanged. Draft-18: aligned full blue-back/face/face/blue-back structures confirm closed kan and four consumed copies; marked river glyphs may use the existing template plus three unanimous train SVM votes agreeing with the primary proposal. Unsplit non-face table art is retained as rejected background evidence. Ambiguous open/added kan and unmarked weak tiles remain unresolved. Draft-19: four matching faces require an independently proven one-called-tile row for daiminkan or an adjacent called pair with a valid three-tile base for kakan. Preserve the added exact tile; ambiguous red/normal layers stay unresolved. Four-seat kan source mappings are explicit. Fitted-face relative geometry handles perspective when glyph orientation is unconfirmed. Thin top stacked bodies use a 16px minimum height; two touching meld faces require neighbour body width and two independently fitted white quadrilaterals. Solid orange backs are detected separately from white bodies and can only join a complete closed-kan row, including coherent side-seat slopes. Two weak faces require network and accepted legacy-template agreement as well as kan geometry; primary network weights and global confidence remain unchanged. Public examples cover all four seats but not every seat/type combination; dark result frames and custom red backs remain unresolved. Draft-20: side-river width splits require a nearly full upright row height, preserving thick sideways riichi bodies. A bounded overlap between adjacent river cells may be cropped only when the neighbour is a geometrically evidenced sideways tile and both cells fit the grid; keep original body boxes in neighbour_crops. This removes a neighbouring riichi glyph from the prior upright classifier crop without changing model weights or acceptance thresholds.",
